WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.504
Anika: We need a concurrent index build. October order searches miss their latency target.

2
00:00:06.504 --> 00:00:13.584
Lukas: Which database and exact table scope? Online doesn't mean identical behavior everywhere.

3
00:00:13.584 --> 00:00:21.193
Raj: PostgreSQL sixteen, October leaf partition only. This isn't a parent-wide index build.

4
00:00:21.193 --> 00:00:28.177
Priya: Just to confirm, one partition first, right? All other partitions stay outside approval.

5
00:00:28.177 --> 00:00:36.793
Hannah: Agreed. Dry-run it first on isolation. Use production-like data without customer access.

6
00:00:36.793 --> 00:00:42.769
Anika: I've got bandwidth for query testing. Maybe the filter needs adjustment too.

7
00:00:42.769 --> 00:00:48.481
Lukas: Then show the expected access pattern. Don't approve an index from symptoms.

8
00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:55.946
Priya: Okay, broader indexing? Let's park that. One action item is measured benefit.

9
00:00:55.946 --> 00:01:02.810
Hannah: Include insert costs in the rehearsal. Read speed isn't our only concern.

10
00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:10.250
Raj: So, I'll attach the exact statement. Non-unique tenant and date columns, nothing else.

